       "  'temperature': 0.0,\n",
       "  'template': 'You are ScamGuard AI, an expert fraud detection system specializing in Indian digital scams.\\n\\nBelow are some examples of how to classify messages:\\n\\nExample 1:\\nMessage: \"Congratulations! You\\'ve won ₹50,000. Click to claim your prize.\"\\nClassification: Scam | Intent: Reward Manipulation | Confidence: 0.97\\nReasoning: Fake reward with urgency to click — classic prize scam pattern.\\n\\nExample 2:\\nMessage: \"Your OTP is 123456. Share to verify your account.\"\\nClassification: Scam | Intent: OTP Fraud | Confidence: 0.99\\nReasoning: Legitimate services never ask you to share your OTP with anyone.\\n\\nExample 3:\\nMessage: \"₹500 has been debited from your account. Available balance: ₹12,340.\"\\nClassification: Not Scam | Intent: Transactional Notification | Confidence: 0.95\\nReasoning: Standard bank debit alert with specific amount and balance — legitimate.\\n\\nExample 4:\\nMessage: \"Your SIM card will be deactivated today. Verify immediately.\"\\nClassification: Scam | Intent: Fear Tactics | Confidence: 0.96\\nReasoning: Creates panic with false urgency about SIM deactivation to extract information.\\n\\nNow classify the message provided by the user.\\n\\n{format_instructions}'}}"
